        "created_at": "2026-11-08T11:35:49.610Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hello,</p>\n<p>My DGX Spark’s internal SSD has dropped three times: “controller is down; will reset: CSTS=0x3”. The second and third drops happened with both workarounds I could find already in place, and the third happened during the Field Diagnostic, which still printed PASS. Should I go straight to an RMA, or is there a fix to try first?</p>\n<p><strong>System</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>DGX Spark Founders Edition, board P4242.</li>\n<li>BIOS 5.36_0ACUM027. <code>fwupdmgr get-updates</code> shows nothing newer.</li>\n<li>DGX OS 7.6.0, kernel 7.0.0-1019-nvidia.</li>\n<li>SSD: Samsung MZALC4T0HBL1-00B07, firmware NXHB202Q, at <code>nvme 0004:01:00.0</code>, root port <code>0004:00:00.0</code> (10de:22ce). Link 32 GT/s x4.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Events</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p><strong>7 Oct 2026, 07:05:</strong> <code>nvme nvme0: controller is down; will reset: CSTS=0x3, PCI_STATUS=0x10</code>. Three READ commands failed with <code>I/O Error (sct 0x3 / sc 0x71)</code>, then the host hung for 2 h 38 min until I power-cycled it. A correctable AER storm on the same link (RxErr, BadTLP, BadDLLP, Rollover, Timeout) reached about 196 errors per second at light load.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>The same day, I applied two workarounds:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>PCIe ASPM policy <code>performance</code>, persisted at boot.</li>\n<li>NVMe APST capped with <code>pm_qos_latency_tolerance_us=5500</code>. <code>set-feature 0x0c</code> is rejected with Invalid Field.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The storm stopped within about 90 s.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>8 Oct to 31 Oct:</strong> small correctable bursts on 7 days, 4 to 97 errors per day, with ASPM still off.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>7 Nov 2026, 22:18:15, with ASPM off and the APST cap active:</strong> the same <code>controller is down; will reset: CSTS=0x3, PCI_STATUS=0x10</code>. Three READ I/O errors (<code>sct 0x3 / sc 0x71</code>). The controller recovered and the host did not hang. There were correctable bursts of 37 and 83 per 6 minutes, both during heavy reads. Counters now: RxErr 1043, BadTLP 170, BadDLLP 16, Rollover 2, Timeout 167.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>8 Nov 2026, 13:34:48, during Field Diagnostic 1.0.9-1, with ASPM off and the APST cap active:</strong> the same <code>controller is down; will reset: CSTS=0x3, PCI_STATUS=0x10</code>. It recovered with no I/O error logged. Link errors ran from 13:34:18 to 13:37:35: RxErr 57,614, BadTLP 7,971, BadDLLP 337, Timeout 6,774 (counter resets at boot; 0 for the two hours before). <code>FioSSD</code> had finished cleanly at 13:33:40 (80 GiB read in 9.5 s, err=0), and the drop came during <code>MemStress</code>, 38 s later. No errors in the next 3 h 48 min at idle.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Field Diagnostic:</strong> PASS, all 8 tests OK with error code 000000000000. I ran 1.0.9-1 because 2.0.4-1 requires DOCA packages (ofed-scripts, mft, opensm, infiniband-diags) that are not installed on this unit. Since FioSSD ended before the fault and no later test checks the SSD, I do not think this PASS clears the drive.</p>\n<p><strong>SSD health:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>critical_warning 0, media_errors 0, percentage_used 0%, 42 °C.</li>\n<li>num_err_log_entries 93; unsafe_shutdowns 8, which are local power cuts.</li>\n<li>No ext4 errors.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Firmware:</strong> the DGX Dashboard offers the “October 2026” update: EC 0x03000508 to 0x03000d07, UEFI device firmware 0x02009b0b to 0x02009e0f and 0x00000516 to 0x00000519, plus about 220 packages. I have not applied it: both controller drops happened on the current versions, and I would like your advice before flashing firmware on a unit with an unstable SSD link.</p>\n<p><strong>Questions</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Is this a known issue with a BIOS, EC or SSD firmware fix? The newest release notes list no NVMe fix, and I found no SSD firmware newer than NXHB202Q.</li>\n<li>The Field Diagnostic passed although the controller dropped during the run. Does the kernel evidence qualify for RMA, or do you need 2.0.4 with DOCA as well? A forum report says those prerequisites replaced the inbox mlx5 driver and left the ConnectX-7 ports unusable.</li>\n<li>Is a Gen4 link-speed cap supported on this slot, as a test?</li>\n<li>Given that it recurs with ASPM off, should I request an RMA through my reseller?</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Similar threads: <a href=\"https://forums.developer.nvidia.com/t/nvme-write-failures-on-dgx-spark/383478\">383478</a> (same SSD and firmware, RMA advised) and <a href=\"https://forums.developer.nvidia.com/t/nvme-write-failures-on-dgx-spark-founders-edition/365094\">365094</a>.</p>\n<p>I can attach <code>nvidia-bug-report</code>, <code>nvme smart-log</code> / <code>error-log</code>, <code>lspci -vv</code> for 0004:01:00.0, and kernel journals.</p>\n<p>Thank you.</p>",
